l_use_result":{"stdout":"---\nrole: lead\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\nnext: [triage:engineer]\nworker: engineer\n---\nThe fix is to make a worker change to any .gitattributes file go to a human, either in the committer's code-path check or as a built-in merge hold, and to name that rule in docs/proposal.md. The change is confined to Go code and the proposal document, so the engineer plans it and the engineer worker implements it.\n\n## Routing\n- triage:engineer: decide where the hold lives (internal/committer/codepath.go or the merger's hold logic), write the steps, and plan tests plus the docs/proposal.md wording that names the rule.\n- worker engineer: Go change with unit tests and the proposal doc update.\n\n## Open issues\n- Agent reviewers already get a raw text diff that ignores attributes (internal/gitx/review.go, internal/reviewer/doc.go). The remaining gap is the collapsed diff that humans see on GitHub, so the plan should cover that and need not rebuild the reviewer diff.\n- One option in the issue is to add .gitattributes to merge.protected_paths in .ard/config.yaml. Agents may not edit that file, so if maintainers want that option instead of a code-level hold, a person has to make the config change.\npackage committer\n\nimport (\n\t\"path\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"unicode\"\n)\n\n// CheckCodePath reports why a worker may not commit p for issue, or nil. It is\n// the one copy of the rule: the worker's diff guard (#33) and CommitCode both\n// call it. Paths must already be canonical; they are rejected, not normalised.\n//\n// Refused: a .git segment, .gitmodules, everything under .ard/ (role, config\n// and issue files; the issue's own go through close-out, not through worker\n// code), everything under .ard-input/ (loop inputs), everything under the\n// root .github/ (not only workflows), and secret-shaped file names. Only the\n// repository-root .github/ is reserved; docs/.github/x is ordinary. The\n// reserved first segments match case-insensitively because a case-insensitive\n// filesystem would fold them.\n//\n// issue is accepted for the message and future use; it does not change the\n// outcome today, because every .ard/ path is refused.\nfunc CheckCodePath(issue int, p string) error {\n\t_ = issue\n\tif p == \"\" {\n\t\treturn reason(\"empty path\")\n\t}\n\tfor _, r := range p {\n\t\tif r == '\\\\' || r < 0x20 || r == 0x7f || r == 0xFFFD || unicode.Is(unicode.Cf, r) {\n\t\t\treturn reason(\"backslash, control or invisible character\")\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif path.Clean(p) != p || strings.HasPrefix(p, \"/\") {\n\t\treturn reason(\"not canonical\")\n\t}\n\tsegs := strings.Split(p, \"/\")\n\tfor _, s := range segs {\n\t\tif s == \".\" || s == \"..\" {\n\t\t\treturn reason(\"not canonical\")\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tfor _, seg := range segs {\n\t\tif strings.EqualFold(seg, \".git\") {\n\t\t\treturn reason(\"contains .git\")\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif len(segs) > 1 {\n\t\tswitch strings.ToLower(segs[0]) {\n\t\tcase \".ard\":\n\t\t\treturn reason(\"under .ard/ (role, config and issue files are not worker code)\")\n\t\tcase \".ard-input\":\n\t\t\treturn reason(\"under .ard-input/ (loop inputs)\")\n\t\tcase \".github\":\n\t\t\treturn reason(\"under .github/\")\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t// A file named like a reserved directory is refused too.\n\tswitch strings.ToLower(segs[0]) {\n\tcase \".ard\", \".ard-input\", \".github\":\n\t\tif len(segs) == 1 {\n\t\t\treturn reason(\"reserved name \" + segs[0])\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif strings.EqualFold(segs[len(segs)-1], \".gitmodules\") {\n\t\treturn reason(\"submodule configuration\")\n\t}\n\tif SecretShaped(p) {\n\t\treturn reason(\"secret-shaped file name\")\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nvar (\n\tsecretExact = map[string]bool{\n\t\t\".env\": true, \".netrc\": true, \"_netrc\": true, \".npmrc\": true, \".pypirc\": true,\n\t\t\".htpasswd\": true, \".git-credentials\": true, \".dockercfg\": true,\n\t\t\"credentials\": true, \"credentials.json\": true,\n\t}\n\tsecretEnvOK       = map[string]bool{\".env.example\": true, \".env.sample\": true, \".env.template\": true}\n\tsecretKeyPrefixes = []string{\"id_rsa\", \"id_dsa\", \"id_ecdsa\", \"id_ed25519\"}\n\tsecretSuffixes    = []string{\".pem\", \".key\", \".p12\", \".pfx\", \".jks\", \".keystore\", \".ppk\", \".kdbx\"}\n\tsecretPairs       = []string{\".aws/credentials\", \".docker/config.json\"}\n)\n\n// SecretShaped reports whether p names a file that usually holds a credential.\nfunc SecretShaped(p string) bool {\n\tp = strings.ToLower(p)\n\tbase := path.Base(p)\n\tif secretExact[base] {\n\t\treturn true\n\t}\n\tif strings.HasPrefix(base, \".env.\") && !secretEnvOK[base] {\n\t\treturn true\n\t}\n\tfor _, pre := range secretKeyPrefixes {\n\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(base, pre) {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif strings.HasPrefix(base, \"service-account\") && strings.HasSuffix(base, \".json\") {\n\t\treturn true\n\t}\n\tfor _, suf := range secretSuffixes {\n\t\tif strings.HasSuffix(base, suf) {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tfor _, pair := range secretPairs {\n\t\tif p == pair || strings.HasSuffix(p, \"/\"+pair) {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\nbranches.go\ncode.go\ncode_test.go\ncodepath.go\ncodepath_test.go\ncommitter.go\ncommitter_test.go\nerrors.go\nguard.go\ninit.go\ninit_test.go\nmessage.go\nrefs.go\nrefs_test.go\nrequest.go\nunit_test.go\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.go\n82:| `ard:needs-approval` | Merger | PR touches a protected path; merges after a human approves |\n229:The starter engineer (`.ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt`) plans for the worker without implementing. Its inputs are `.ard-input/<issue#>/issue.md`, `comments.md` and `.ard/<issue#>/plan.md`, all untrusted. It writes the `## Implementation` section of `plan.md` with Steps, Test plan, Risk and Size, sized S, M, L or XL on a scale tied to the worker's 1,000-line guard (XL is 1,000 lines or more). It writes `triage-engineer.md` with `role: engineer` and `attempt: 1`, never a `worker` key. It answers `needs-human` for an XL change, a chan