{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017ha1mMHdzKZ9SbT34Cy9bj","type":"tool_result","content":"internal/roles/worker_engineer_test.go:74:\t\t\".github/\", \".gitmodules\", \"1,000\", \"256\", \"1 MiB\", \"symlink\", \"binary\", \"at run time\",\ninternal/roles/workers/engineer/prompt.txt:59:  .ard-input/, any path with a .git segment, and .gitmodules;\ninternal/committer/codepath.go:13:// Refused: a .git segment, .gitmodules, everything under .ard/ (role, config\ninternal/committer/codepath.go:64:\tif strings.EqualFold(segs[len(segs)-1], \".gitmodules\") {\ninternal/committer/codepath_test.go:9:\t\t\".ard-input/12/issue.md\", \"a/.git/hooks/x\", \"a/.GIT/x\", \".gitmodules\", \"sub/.gitmodules\",\ninternal/worker/unit_test.go:87:\trejects := []Change{rc(\"a\"), rc(\".github/CODEOWNERS\"), rc(\".github/workflows/x.yml\"), rc(\".ard/config.yaml\"), rc(\".ard/workers/x/prompt.txt\"), rc(\".ard/8/plan.md\"), rc(\".env\"), rc(\"x/.git/config\"), rc(\".gitmodules\")}\ndocs/proposal.md:300:5. **Guard the diff** after each agent or fix step, before anything leaves the host. The worktree belongs to the agent, so the guard never trusts its `.git`, config, index or attributes: git runs against the controller's own clone with a private index filled from the base commit (so `skip-worktree` and `assume-unchanged` hide nothing, and no planted filter, textconv, fsmonitor or hook runs), with its objects in a private temp directory (the clone is only read, so an agent cannot grow it); a worktree with a new or resized file over 1 MiB, or more than 256 of them, is held before anything is hashed. The scanned bytes are copied to a controller-private directory and the code lane commits the copies, so nothing can change a file between the scan and the commit. Close-out's changed-file listing uses the same hardened path. Paths under `.ard/<issue#>/` and `.ard-input/` belong to close-out and the loop and are left out. Everything else is checked, and any rejection holds the job for a human (`ard:needs-human`, nothing pushed): the path rule in `committer.CheckCodePath` (all of `.github/`, the rest of `.ard/`, `.git` segments, `.gitmodules`, secret-shaped names), any symlink, nested repository or other non-regular file, a file over 1 MiB, a binary file, and more than 256 changed files. The credential scan runs twice: the content of every written file is checked for the values of known secrets (the hold names the variable, never the value), and the built-in pattern scanner runs over it with only the findings on lines this job added kept, so a worker that edits a file that already holds a credential-shaped fixture is not held for lines it did not write. The comment names file, line and rule (`internal/foo_test.go:12: secret scan rule aws-access-key`), never the text. A scanner error fails closed. Test fixtures that look like credentials must be built at run time, as `internal/redact`'s tests do (`\"AK\" + \"IA\" + ...`); a literal is held, and there is no in-band escape. Over 1,000 changed lines in the whole PR (the diff against the merge base with `main`) also holds. The comment shows the reason as `diff guard: <entry>; <entry>; <entry>; and N more`.\npackage committer\n\nimport \"testing\"\n\nfunc TestCheckCodePath(t *testing.T) {\n\trefused := []string{\n\t\t\".github/workflows/ci.yml\", \".github/CODEOWNERS\", \".GitHub/x\",\n\t\t\".ard/config.yaml\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/12/worker-engineer.md\", \".ARD/Config.yaml\",\n\t\t\".ard-input/12/issue.md\", \"a/.git/hooks/x\", \"a/.GIT/x\", \".gitmodules\", \"sub/.gitmodules\",\n\t\t\".\", \"..\", \"../x\", \"a/../../x\", \"../../etc/passwd\", \".git\\u200c/x\", \".github\\u200b/x\", \"a\\ufffd\", \"./a\", \"a//b\", \"/abs\", \"a\\\\b\", \"a\\x01b\", \"\", \".github\", \".ard\",\n\t\t// secret-shaped\n\t\t\".env\", \"config/.env.prod\", \"certs/server.pem\", \"id_ed25519.pub\", \".aws/credentials\",\n\t\t\"x/.docker/config.json\", \"service-account-pr