{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChKvgv8yAYgbDmEat2Eh6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the plan for #142 to `.ard/142/plan.md` and the triage comment to `.ard/142/triage-engineer.md`. Nothing was run or built; this is planning only.\n\nThe plan puts the rule in `committer.CheckCodePath`. A worker change to any `.gitattributes` file, at any depth and in any letter case, would be refused. That path check is shared by the worker's diff guard and the committer's `CommitCode`, so a rejection already holds the job for a human with nothing pushed.\n\nI did not use `merge.protected_paths`, because the design says that list has no code-level floor and `.ard/config.yaml` can't be edited by agents. Agent reviewers already get a diff that ignores attributes, so that part needs no change.\n\nThe steps cover six files:\n- **Code and tests:** the check in `internal/committer/codepath.go`, plus new cases in `codepath_test.go` and `internal/worker/unit_test.go`.\n- **Worker prompt:** the engineer worker's starter prompt and its test.\n- **Docs:** `docs/proposal.md`, naming the rule.\n\nSize is S and risk is low. The one behaviour change is that a worker can no longer make a legitimate `.gitattributes` edit, such as line-ending settings, without a human.\n\nI did not check whether `merge.protected_paths` in `.ard/config.yaml` covers the starter prompt file the plan changes, so the plan tells the worker to check that before starting."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1738,"cache_read_input_tokens":18650,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1738},"output_tokens":483,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75249968-4510-4f